      "extractedText": "BabelStone Ideographic Description Sequences (IDS)\n\nMaintained by: Andrew West (魏安)\nFile Date: 2025-06-27; Unicode Version: 16.0\nOriginal source: https://babelstone.co.uk/CJK/IDS.TXT\nMirror revision: 6d0989b007bdfa566a864419448b125799ef5f9f\nSHA-256: cc2a0a97e6a51ed6ebe59870ef2af66e83f3c3c27387d79b4441bb2d791d78b1\n\nThe following statement is copied from documentation item 2 in the pinned\nIDS.TXT used by Mojidata. It is the upstream use/waiver statement, not CC0.\n\n# 2. Under U.S. copyright law, data (i.e. a collection of facts) is not eligible to copyright protection (see\n#\t<https://sco.library.emory.edu/research-data-management/publishing/copyright-data.html>), and as IDS descriptions\n#\tfor CJK ideographs are facts not original creative compositions, IDS sequences in themselves are not eligible for\n#\tcopyright protection (that is to say, you could no more copyright 彼 = ⿰彳皮 than you could copyright 1 + 1 = 2).\n#\tTherefore, anyone is free to make use of the IDS data provided in this file for personal or commercial purposes\n#\twithout asking permission or providing attribution. I furthermore waive any copyright claims to the presentation\n#\tformat of the IDS data used in this file, so anyone is free to fork the file, or use it as the basis for a new IDS\n#\tdata set.\n#\n\nMojidata parses the source into ids and ids_comment tables and adds IDS\nfrom the separately licensed Mojidata IDS inputs.\n",
