      "extractedText": "常用漢字表 / 在留カード等に係る漢字氏名の表記等に関する告示\n\nSource government notices:\n- 常用漢字表（平成22年内閣告示第2号）\n  https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/kanji/\n- 在留カード等に係る漢字氏名の表記等に関する告示\n  （平成23年法務省告示第582号）別表第四の一・二\n  https://www.moj.go.jp/isa/content/930002422.pdf\n\nBasis: Japan's Copyright Act, Article 13, item 2 (著作権法第13条第2号).\nGovernment notices are excluded from the rights provided in Chapter II.\nhttps://laws.e-gov.go.jp/law/345AC0000000048\nThis reference is to item 2 of Article 13, not to an Article 13-2.\n\nMojidata imports the extracted JSON data from these pinned npm packages:\n- @mandel59/joyokanjihyo 1.2.1 (joyokanjihyo.json)\n- @mandel59/nyukanseiji 1.2.1 (nyukanseiji.json)\n\nThe corrected upstream source declarations are preserved byte for byte from:\n- sources/joyo-README.md:\n  https://github.com/mandel59/joyokanjihyo/blob/e6bbe8a0ea2648f9c4001b43f4b0fdafc6b7ec37/README.md\n- sources/nyukan-README.md:\n  https://github.com/mandel59/nyukanseiji/blob/3ecf5860ea0755dae5933361f5ca9c6930523956/README.md\n\nThe pinned npm 1.2.1 packages include these corrected declarations. The patch\nreleases correct the Article 13, item 2 reference and update the e-Gov link;\ntheir JSON data and type definitions are byte-identical to npm 1.2.0.\nData versions above identify the imported datasets; the separate README\nrevisions identify the original documentation fixes.\nTheir MIT-0 statements concern the extraction programs. Mojidata imports the\ngovernment-notice data, not those extraction programs.\n\nAffected data: joyo, joyo_acceptable, joyo_kangxi; nyukan_itaiji, nyukan_ruiji,\nand the nyukan view. The JSON is normalized into SQLite tables.\n",
